            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0944" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003 C 73/7</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chinese Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sze</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to your
                    communication of April 13, 1922, and my letter of acknowledgment of the 25th of
                    the same month, I am now enabled to inform you that according to advices
                    received from the appropriate diplomatic officers of the United States, all the
                    Powers concerned have given their assent to the postponement of the meeting of
                    the committee on extraterritoriality, as requested by your Government in order
                    that it may complete the work of a technical character needed.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>[For the Secretary of State:]<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
